        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 737,
        "paragraph_id": "44886040",
        "text": "Finally the drag coefficient (Cd) is calculated with Equation (2.88). A drag coefficient is used to determine the equilibrium sediment concentrations (equation 2.89). On top of that Souslby (1997) gives a relation between the bed shear stress of the depth-averaged current speed."
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 30057,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 833,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 741,
        "paragraph_id": "1C454AAD",
        "text": "In this equation z0 is used for the bed roughness length and is used as zero flow velocity level in the formulation of the sediment concentration. In XBeach this is a fixed value (keyword: z0), but Soulsby (1997) argues there is a relation between the Nikuradse and kinematic viscosity."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 30090,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 834,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 742,
        "paragraph_id": "294E7E6E",
        "text": "Van Thiel-Van Rijn"
      }
    ],
